20622	{"artifactId":"LLD-9b4a74dcdf47852a-s1","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-9b4a74dcdf47852a-s1-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-08T16:36:47.911Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The Story has no upstream definition with acceptance criteria, so the single ac1 standing for the stakeholder request (a per-Story artifact that lists tests with their execution status, used by the gate) is the whole intent, and the design covers it without building a non-goal.","evidence":"Glob of .insrc/artifacts/*9b4a74dc* returns only LLD-9b4a74dcdf47852a-s1.json: no DEF, ISSUE, SPEC or HLD exists for this work item. The design's sections 2 to 6 cover the mapping input, the gate running the files, per-title results, the TESTS record and its link from BUILD. No non-goals are stated upstream to violate. The design's open question 3 already flags that ac1 is a stand-in. [files: .insrc/artifacts/LLD-9b4a74dcdf47852a-s1.json]","action":"None. Open question 3 (is the request itself the acceptance criterion) still needs the user's answer before plan.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Today the gate finds test files only through a leading '<file>.test.ts:' prefix, runs all files in one command and reads only the exit code. An unprefixed plan test name fails the check, and the small standalone route drops unprefixed subjects and reports 'the LLD names no test file' when none has a prefix.","evidence":"validation-checks.ts:76 `LEADING_TEST_FILE = /^\\s*([A-Za-z0-9_.-]+\\.test\\.ts)\\s*:/`; :214 `runOne(repoPath, [...plan.testCommand, ...plan.testFiles], plan.testTimeoutMs, deps)` (one command); :191 `ok: r.exitCode === 0`; :215-219 unresolved names force `ok: false`; :144-146 `names.filter(n => LEADING_TEST_FILE.test(n))` then `noTests: { ok: false, note: 'the LLD names no test file' }`; :165 trivial route `noTests: { ok: true, ... }`. [files: src/mcp/build-step/validation-checks.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"In the validate turn a judge failure returns 'verdict-session-timeout', 'unparseable-verdict' or 'verdict-session-failed' before the BUILD record is written. testsPassed comes from the gate's results. The standalone flag counts the caller's declaration only when the work item has no definition head.","evidence":"validate.ts:249-262 returns the three error codes inside the judge try/catch and after judgeShapeError, all before the persist block at :285-381. :264 `const testsPassed = results.tests.ok`. :330-333 `const noHead = Object.keys(readEpicDefinitionCore(repoPath, epicHash)).length === 0; ... inheritedStoryStandalone(repoPath, epicHash, storyId, ident.standalone !== undefined && noHead ? true : undefined)`. The checks run at :237, before the judge, so a test-record write between them is possible as designed. [files: src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The BUILD record's paths come from pathsForMerged on the merged record's own createdAt, not from storyRecordFolderArgs. Its three writers (validate turn, ensureBuildRecordOnCompletion, trivial implement turn) all go through persistBuildRecord and mergeWithPrior, and each stamps the current time on a first write. storyRecordFolderArgs has one caller, the code-review writer.","evidence":"standalone-record.ts:244-256 pathsForMerged calls `buildRecordFolderArgs(..., standalone, merged.meta.createdAt)`; :271 and :294 both call mergeWithPrior; :352 `if (prior === null) return rec` (the seeding point the design names). Grep for `persistBuildRecord(` / `persistStandaloneBuildRecord(` outside tests: validate.ts:371, completion-record.ts:85, implement.ts:159 only, each with `createdAt: now` / `new Date().toISOString()`. Grep for storyRecordFolderArgs: defined storage.ts:445, used only in code-review/subject-paths.ts:32. storage.ts:451-453 anchors on the persisted BUILD record's `createdAt` and `standalone`. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/code-review/subject-paths.ts, src/mcp/build-step/phases/implement.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.4","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The TAP reporter prints what section 3.3 says: one 'ok N - title' / 'not ok N - title' line per test and per suite, four spaces per depth, ' # SKIP' with optional reason and ' # TODO', '#' as '\\#' and backslash as '\\\\', quotes unchanged, and a parent after its children as 'not ok' when a child failed.","evidence":"tap-sample/sample.tap: line 35 `ok 3 - skipped by option # SKIP`, 41 `ok 4 - skipped with reason # SKIP needs env`, 47 `ok 5 - todo one # TODO`, 53 `ok 6 - has \\# hash and \\\\ backslash and \"double\" and 'single' quotes`, 59/65 `ok 7 - dup title` / `not ok 8 - dup title`, 86 `    ok 1 - nested pass`, 93 `        not ok 1 - deep fail`, 116 `    not ok 2 - inner suite`, 126 `not ok 9 - outer suite`. sample-source.txt matches these titles. Not checked: the Node version of the capture. One gap the design does not state: YAML diagnostic text sits at the same four-space indent as a depth-1 result line (sample.tap line 16), so the parser should skip the `---` to `...` blocks and read stdout only, or an error message that begins 'ok N - ' could be read as a title. [files: docs/standalone/add-test-record-artifact-build-flow-E202610089b4a74dc/S001/tap-sample/sample.tap, docs/standalone/add-test-record-artifact-build-flow-E202610089b4a74dc/S001/tap-sample/sample-source.txt]","action":"State in the LLD that diagnostic blocks are skipped and that titles are parsed from stdout only, with a fixture for it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"What the design calls new does not exist yet (the 'TESTS' kind, a TESTS artifact id, NotApprovableError, the `tests` input field), and the pieces it reuses exist with the stated shape (ArtifactKind and STORY_SCOPED in path-scheme.ts, resolveArtifactMdPath, the insrc:artifact marker and jsonPathForMd).","evidence":"path-scheme.ts:46 `export type ArtifactKind = 'SPEC' | 'DEF' | 'HLD' | 'LLD' | 'PLAN' | 'BUILD' | 'CR' | 'EXT' | 'ISSUE'` and :68 STORY_SCOPED `['LLD', 'PLAN', 'BUILD', 'CR', 'EXT']`: no TESTS. storage.ts artifact-id functions (:148-173, :663) have none for TESTS. gates.ts (read in full) declares ArtifactMissingError, ArtifactNotApprovedError, ReviewBlockedError, NoPendingArtifactsError and no NotApprovableError. types.ts:59-81 BuildStepInputValidate has no `tests`; server.ts:563-587 inputSchema has none. storage.ts:475 `ARTIFACT_ID_MARKER_RE = /<!--\\s*insrc:artifact\\s+([A-Za-z0-9._-]+)\\s*-->/` accepts a TESTS id, so gates.ts:973-991 jsonPathForMd resolves TESTS.md to its json. [files: src/workflow/path-scheme.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/mcp/build-step/types.ts, src/mcp/server.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Plan Tasks' tests carry a level from 'unit', 'integration', 'live', 'smoke', and a standalone design's test strategy may also use 'contract', so the 'live'/'smoke' rule for reported results can be applied on both routes.","evidence":"artifacts/plan.ts:45 `export type TestLevel = 'unit' | 'integration' | 'live' | 'smoke'` with :48 `readonly level: TestLevel`; artifacts/lld.ts:113 `readonly level: 'unit' | 'integration' | 'live' | 'smoke' | 'contract'`. render.ts:93 already reads `t.level` off the Task's tests. Today's planTaskCheckPlan (validation-checks.ts:129) and smallStandaloneCheckPlan (:141) type only `name` / `subjects`, so adding the optional `level` is a widening. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/plan.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/lld.ts, src/mcp/build-step/validation-checks.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The inventory of readers of the artifacts directory and of places that list the kinds is complete, and each behaves today as section 3.5 says.","evidence":"Grep for readdir across src, vscode-plugin/src and jetbrains-plugin/src/main, crossed with files naming the artifacts directory, gives: gates.ts:145 (DEF regex) and :786 (`^(DEF|HLD|LLD|PLAN|BUILD)-`), pending.ts:110-115 (PENDING_KINDS filter), locate/ownership.ts:85, questions.ts:538-539 (prefix filter), tracker/resolve.ts (anchored DEF/ISSUE/LLD/PLAN regexes), cli/services/workflow.ts:129 (DEF_RE), amendments/staleness.ts:72-74 and store.ts:69-71, :199-201 (AMD prefix), delivery/load.ts:139-150, migrate-docs-tree.ts:320, vscode-plugin daemon-gateway.ts:95, WorkflowChainReader.kt. All are in the design's list. indexer/index.ts and daemon/index.ts match the search but read other directories (extension.ts:278 reads the log dir). Grep for kind alternations finds only path-scheme.ts:68, migrate-docs-tree.ts:109, gates.ts:784, delivery/load.ts:33, all listed. resolve-comment.ts:96 `ARTIFACT_ID_RE = /^(DEF|HLD|LLD)-.../` returns null for a TESTS id. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/pending.ts, src/workflow/questions.ts, src/workflow/tracker/resolve.ts, src/workflow/amendments/store.ts, src/workflow/amendments/staleness.ts, src/workflow/resolve-comment.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Approval and rejection stamps are written only by approveArtifactByJsonPath and rejectArtifactByJsonPath, which today stamp any json with a meta. approveOne runs the code-review gate first for any meta with an Epic and a Story. The batch matches only DEF, HLD, LLD, PLAN and BUILD.","evidence":"gates.ts:565-634 approveArtifactByJsonPath checks only `typeof artifact.meta !== 'object'` before stamping; :942-960 rejectArtifactByJsonPath likewise. :819-829 approveOne: `if (meta !== undefined && meta.epicHash !== undefined && meta.storyId !== undefined) { const gate = enforceCodeReviewGate(...); codeReview.push(...)` runs before :837. :784 batch regex `^(DEF|HLD|LLD|PLAN|BUILD)-`. Callers outside tests: gates.ts:837, cli/services/workflow.ts:158 and :172, and daemon/index.ts:652 (approveWorkflowTarget). Grep for other writers of approvedAt/rejectedAt finds only amendments/store.ts (AMD records). A kind check in the two functions plus one at the top of approveOne therefore covers every route. [files: src/workflow/gates.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.3","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The build tool's input shape is registered in src/mcp/server.ts, handler.ts only dispatches on the phase, and the check plans, the runner and renderCheckEvidence each have one production caller in validate.ts.","evidence":"server.ts:563-587 holds the zod inputSchema for insrc_build_step (phase, target, repo, epicHash, standalone, summary) and :589 passes rawArgs to handleBuildStep. handler.ts:40-44 casts the input and switches on `step.phase` with no shape of its own. Grep outside tests: planTaskCheckPlan only at validate.ts:167, smallStandaloneCheckPlan at :201, runValidationChecks at :237 (via the override), renderCheckEvidence at :248, handleValidate only at handler.ts:44. Note for the plan: existing tests inject results through `_setBuildValidateCheckRunnerForTests` (validate.ts:57-64); those stand-ins return a tests result without the new `files` and `namedTests`, and tsc does not check test files, so the new code must tolerate their absence or the stand-ins must be updated. [files: src/mcp/server.ts, src/mcp/build-step/handler.ts, src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts]","action":"Add the existing check-runner stand-ins in build-step.test.ts to the change sites, or state that the evidence and record code treat missing `files`/`namedTests` as empty.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.4","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The VS Code plugin's workflowChain lists a row for every json in the artifacts directory, 'pending' unless stamped, so it must skip TESTS. The JetBrains reader only reads DEF, HLD, LLD and AMD names and needs no change.","evidence":"daemon-gateway.ts:102-114: `if (!entry.endsWith('.json')) continue;` then for every entry `rows.push({ slug: parsed.meta?.epicSlug ?? entry.replace(/\\.json$/, ''), stage: stageFromFilename(entry), status: parsed.meta?.approvedAt !== undefined ? 'approved' : 'pending' })`. WorkflowChainReader.kt:102 `.filter { it.startsWith(\"DEF-\") && it.endsWith(\".json\") }`, :116 reads `HLD-$epicHash.json`, :156 `LLD-$epicHash-$storyId.json`, :193-203 the `AMD-$epicHash-` prefix. [files: vscode-plugin/src/panels/daemon-gateway.ts, jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/workflow/WorkflowChainReader.kt]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.5","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The change log has two writers that each hand-list the workflow's own files, and the change-set derivation returns the working tree's files as soon as any non-excluded file is dirty, so the test record's files must be in both lists.","evidence":"validate.ts:367-368 `exclude: [own.json, own.md, buildStartRelPath(epicHash, storyId)]`; completion-record.ts:75 the same three. changed-files.ts:137-138 `const kept = keep(working); if (kept.length > 0) return kept;` before the committed-range fallback at :143. A TESTS json or TESTS.md written before the judge and left out of either list would be the returned set. The trivial implement writer (implement.ts:159-168) writes no changeLog. [files: src/mcp/build-step/phases/validate.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/completion-record.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/changed-files.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The docs-tree migration holds its own kind pattern and its own story-scoped list, and it converges already-nested documents, so a TESTS.md it does not know would be left behind in a forked folder. Adding TESTS to both makes it converge with its Story.","evidence":"migrate-docs-tree.ts:109 `/^(SPEC|DEF|HLD|LLD|PLAN|BUILD|CR|EXT|ISSUE)-([0-9a-f]{16})(?:-(.+))?$/` and :115 `const storyScoped = kind === 'LLD' || kind === 'PLAN' || kind === 'BUILD' || kind === 'CR' || kind === 'EXT'`, separate from path-scheme. :324 `if (parsed === null) continue;` drops an unknown id. :142-164 indexNestedMd indexes nested md by marker, so a marker-bearing TESTS.md is found once the id parses; :421-467 moves each member to resolveArtifactMdPath. Companion moves at :499-500 skip `.md`, so an unknown TESTS.md really would stay behind. Residual: :432-437 marks a member whose md is missing as unmappable, so a TESTS json written without its md would join that list (same as BUILD today). [files: src/workflow/migrate-docs-tree.ts]","action":"Have the test-record writer treat json and md as one write for error reporting, so a json without an md is not left on disk.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The separate IDE fork (insors-ai/insrc-ide) tolerates a BUILD record with a new optional body field and a new TESTS json in the artifacts directory.","evidence":"The fork is a separate repository and is not in this working directory; CLAUDE.md says only that it mirrors IPC types. I could check this repository's side only: BuildRecord.body gains one optional field (standalone-record.ts:76-96 shows the current optional-field body) and the verdict's evidence only gains fields. The design states the same gap in its backward-compat note and open question 4. [files: src/workflow/runners/build/standalone-record.ts]","action":"Decide open question 4: who checks the fork's BUILD reader and artifact listing, and whether that holds the Story's last Task.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The failures the design handles are detectable with the existing primitives: the process runner never rejects and reports spawn errors, timeouts and exit codes with the whole output; the delivery loader reports an unknown prefix as an 'unknown-kind' failure (so a skip is needed); and the ownership scan does not fail on a record with no citations.","evidence":"process-group.ts:56-93: `Never rejects`; stdout and stderr are accumulated without a cap (:85-86), `timedOut` set at :83, `spawnError` at :89, so 'nothing is cut' is achievable and the 4,000-character cut is only validation-checks.ts:34/173-175 `tail`. validation-checks.ts:185-190 maps spawnError and timedOut to failed results with notes. delivery/load.ts:148-150 `if (kindOfFile(fileName) === null) { failures.push({ fileName, reason: 'unknown-kind', ... }); continue; }`. ownership.ts:95 `const citations = Array.isArray(parsed.citations) ? parsed.citations : [];`. validate.ts:375-380 already swallows a BUILD persist failure, the pattern the test-record write follows. [files: src/shared/process-group.ts, src/mcp/build-step/validation-checks.ts, src/workflow/delivery/load.ts, src/workflow/locate/ownership.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ac1 maps to tests, the existing test files the subjects are prefixed with exist under __tests__ folders (so today's gate resolves them), render.test.ts is the name of exactly two files, and the live subject's source mapping has the shape step 7 converts from.","evidence":"The acceptance mapping gives ac1 three proving tests (one build-step, one validation-checks, one live). Glob finds src/mcp/build-step/__tests__/{build-step,render,validation-checks}.test.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/__tests__/render.test.ts (the second render.test.ts), src/workflow/__tests__/migrate-docs-tree.test.ts, src/workflow/runners/build/__tests__/{build-record,completion-record}.test.ts and vscode-plugin/src/panels/__tests__/daemon-gateway.test.ts (uses node:test, line 6). tap-results, test-mapping, test-record and artifact-kinds test files do not exist yet, as expected for new files. tests.map.json has `\"t1\": [ { \"planTest\": ..., \"cases\": [{\"file\", \"title\"}], \"mutations\": [...] } ]`, matching the conversion (rename planTest to name, drop mutations). Not run: whether the vscode-plugin test passes when started from the repository root by the gate. [files: docs/epics/make-insrc-analysis-complete-used-right-E20261006b9d5c5c4/S007/tests.map.json, vscode-plugin/src/panels/__tests__/daemon-gateway.test.ts, src/mcp/build-step/__tests__/render.test.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/companion/__tests__/render.test.ts]","action":"Before plan, run `npx tsx --test vscode-plugin/src/panels/__tests__/daemon-gateway.test.ts` once from the repository root to confirm the gate can run it there.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":16,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-08T16:36:47.911Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
